<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:29:02Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Midterms 2026: Georgians on the front lines of the people’s war against data centres</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bf4519a0322d0a172dc839bad5ad045d8d4c213603015f4787af460052355c7b</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:28:41Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T06:11:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261102-midterms-2026-georgians-front-lines-people-war-against-data-centres--f7902fa87f3b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261102-midterms-2026-georgians-front-lines-people-war-against-data-centres" /><summary type="html">Artificial intelligence emerged as a major issue on the 2026 US midterm campaign trail, with opposition to data centres drawing supporters across partisan divides united over ecological worries, increased utility bills and business interests outweighing citizen concerns. Georgia, the top US market for data centre construction, has been on the front line of the struggle.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Halloween weekend shootings across US leave at least six dead, dozens wounded</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:79ec75ad256520e5111e5eac873516aa568ead7242625777cfa1c16e519cd4f7</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:28:47Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T00:49:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261102-halloween-weekend-shootings-across-us-leave-at-least-six-dead-dozens-wounded--acbd7ff7fa9d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261102-halloween-weekend-shootings-across-us-leave-at-least-six-dead-dozens-wounded" /><summary type="html">A spate of shootings in nightlife districts and near university campuses across the United States over Halloween weekend left at least six people dead and dozens wounded, with Dallas recording the highest toll. Police were investigating multiple incidents in several states, while some suspects remained at large.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Nine killed as business jet crashes into South Florida neighbourhood</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e2a435a6c18678d0e1c9cffc195946b6eb44c11717e3dac91280fe22d67bed4a</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:28:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T23:45:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261101-nine-killed-as-business-jet-crashes-into-south-florida-neighbourhood--8c4ca3ac05fd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261101-nine-killed-as-business-jet-crashes-into-south-florida-neighbourhood" /><summary type="html">A business jet plunged into a South Florida neighbourhood on Sunday, killing all nine people aboard and exploding into a fireball near homes and a busy road. The pilot had reported icing, precipitation and severe turbulence before the Learjet entered a steep dive, according to air traffic control recordings.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Michigan ‘Betrayal’ &amp; Mid Term Manouvres</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:414ef35cfb66f105ef4176fb36041cff7cb7eefee78b5147951edcdb47f874c2</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:29:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T19:37:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261101-michigan-betrayal-mid-term-manouvres--587c9df436b5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261101-michigan-betrayal-mid-term-manouvres" /><summary type="html">France 24’s Spotlight Presenter Gavin Lee assesses the last minute campaign dramas and takes an US election overview on the ‘must watch states’ alongside Professor Donald Green, Professor of Political Science at Columbia University and co-author of the definitive book ‘Get Out the Vote’, and foreign affairs analyst Laurie Dundon, who previously served in the U.S. State Department during the Clinton administration.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>US Midterms: Democrats face leftward surge</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7bc638e5477a475af5641012e055105904822651625a7889543d9f34467931d0</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T13:56:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-democrats-face-leftward-surge--a5f145f073e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-democrats-face-leftward-surge" /><summary type="html">As Democrats seek to regain control of Congress, divisions within the party are emerging over its future direction. A new wave of progressive candidates is pushing to shift priorities further to the left, challenging corporate money in politics and calling for universal healthcare, climate action and an end to police violence. Monte Francis reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Midterms: Affordability at heart of Michigan race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d731700caee8db24f95f3d16045bfef1440b45ac130f5314c0deab5c37945918</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T09:39:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-affordability-at-heart-of-michigan-race--ad6ada0d04e8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-affordability-at-heart-of-michigan-race" /><summary type="html">For many voters, the cost of living is the single biggest issue. Our reporters Jessica Le Masurier and Sarah Andersen travelled to Michigan to meet voters, where, according to one NGO, around 40% of the population struggle to afford basic necessities.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump vs MAGA: Why his movement is splitting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:408a8c87f0c175769b7f4b068967fe690a887435b22fd79a57fe2b045bfe5b61</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T10:11:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261031-trump-vs-maga-why-his-movement-is-splitting--4267dc0a4776.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261031-trump-vs-maga-why-his-movement-is-splitting" /><summary type="html">As the 2026 midterm elections approach, divisions within the MAGA camp are becoming increasingly visible. From the war in Iran and rising fuel prices to the Epstein files, several of Trump’s decisions are fuelling divisions among his most loyal supporters.
 
Once united by a shared vision of America, MAGA now brings together factions that increasingly disagree over foreign policy, the economy and what “America First” should actually mean. Yet Trump remains the central figure holding this political coalition together – and he is fighting to keep it that way.
 
Why are some of the president’s longtime allies distancing themselves from him? Can MAGA remain united despite these disagreements? And can Trump still mobilise his base ahead of the midterms?
 
🔍 Our journalist Stella Elgersma breaks down the divisions within the MAGA movement and Donald Trump’s strategy to rally his supporters, once again.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Atmosphere of fear': Trump moves to curtail voting rights ahead of the midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:296e2e3b5ef7c62637b0429d69092dd10407f3180796d10cfd7c0a217d2c32db</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T09:40:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261031-united-states-atmosphere-of-fear-trump-moves-to-curtail-voting-rights-ahead-of-the-midterms--ef0cd17927a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261031-united-states-atmosphere-of-fear-trump-moves-to-curtail-voting-rights-ahead-of-the-midterms" /><summary type="html">Americans vote on November 3 in midterm elections that could see Republicans lose control of Congress, endangering US President Donald Trump's legislative agenda. Under the US Constitution, elections are organized by the respective states – but that has not halted US President Donald Trump from trying to wield his influence ahead of the vote.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Flavio Bolsonaro posts video, says he fled Brazil due to ‘persecution’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c7cb0dc0ab6d2bdb30edcf2da4cd800a15f4abc33cfab1a38b629f267e9def5f</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T06:25:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261031-flavio-bolsonaro-posts-video-says-he-fled-brazil-due-to-persecution--3ad01377532f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261031-flavio-bolsonaro-posts-video-says-he-fled-brazil-due-to-persecution" /><summary type="html">Brazil's defeated right-wing presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro posted a video message on social media late Friday to declare he had fled to the US because he was a victim of 'persecution'. Bolsonaro, who lost Sunday's election runoff to President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva, gave no details of how he left the country.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump admin approves potential Patriot missiles sale to Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6c8c74aa0582b48f388b43b035f9577c4d16fcce8743f364ecbeccfb6d8b0511</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T23:19:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261030-trump-admin-approves-potential-patriot-missiles-sale-to-ukraine--23216ec77f01.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261030-trump-admin-approves-potential-patriot-missiles-sale-to-ukraine" /><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>MAGA: Why Trump's movement is fracturing?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d5b54d382d016282720c68679b22b9a4ebcc6a72e35198a50ad03cd823d1d73</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T18:01:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-maga-why-trump-s-movement-is-fracturing--e5d6b934be9d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-maga-why-trump-s-movement-is-fracturing" /><summary type="html">As the 2026 midterm elections approach, divisions within the MAGA camp are becoming increasingly visible. From the war in Iran and rising fuel prices to the Epstein files, several of Trump’s decisions are fuelling divisions among his most loyal supporters.
 
Once united by a shared vision of America, MAGA now brings together factions that increasingly disagree over foreign policy, the economy and what “America First” should actually mean. Yet Trump remains the central figure holding this political coalition together – and he is fighting to keep it that way.
 
Why are some of the president’s longtime allies distancing themselves from him? Can MAGA remain united despite these disagreements? And can Trump still mobilise his base ahead of the midterms?
 
🔍 Our journalist Stella Elgersma breaks down the divisions within the MAGA movement and Donald Trump’s strategy to rally his supporters, once again.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Deeply hurt': Convicted murderer Christa Pike speaks out after botched execution</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ebe61b7c17d5eff0e9802cd6b0e34c93666f751a6d1415ab304651d747a02b73</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T15:29:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261030-deeply-hurt-convicted-murderer-christa-pike-speaks-out-after-botched-execution--142643fa6707.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261030-deeply-hurt-convicted-murderer-christa-pike-speaks-out-after-botched-execution" /><summary type="html">Tennessee death row inmate Christa Pike said she remains in constant pain after surviving a botched lethal injection in September, in her first public statement since the failed execution. She expressed gratitude for those who saved her life while urging compassion for her victim's family.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>How will the women's vote shape the US midterms?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:88a4ab5c7266bac86f7ab98cc45f13fd513b39ccf18236eff2699550ef02c12c</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T13:52:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261030-how-will-the-women-s-vote-shape-the-us-midterms--b24f5ee96a41.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261030-how-will-the-women-s-vote-shape-the-us-midterms" /><summary type="html">With the US midterms approaching, we examine the power of the women's vote in an election that will shape the balance of power in Washington during Donald Trump’s final two years in office. Annette Young talks to Annie Karni, congressional correspondent for The New York Times and Kelly Dittmar, Director of Research at the Centre for American Women and Politics.</summary><category term="The 51%" /></entry><entry><title>Texas Republicans accused of changing electoral rules ahead of midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dfc4aad6897a55c2bd677acf464a2077e3815fd083ff8038c68ef0ea7a82f192</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T13:07:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261030-texas-republicans-accused-of-changing-electoral-rules-ahead-of-midterms--6f6bffa6894f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261030-texas-republicans-accused-of-changing-electoral-rules-ahead-of-midterms" /><summary type="html">With the US midterm elections approaching, Republicans in Texas are being accused of changing electoral rules in their favour. In Tarrant County, near Dallas, they've cut the number of election-day polling places by nearly 30 percent. The decision is being challenged in court and adds to last year's state-wide redistricting, a move designed to benefit Republicans. But the measures could also help galvanise the Democratic opposition. FRANCE 24's Pierrick Leurent reports, with Wassim Cornet.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>‘Scared of crossing the border’: The Arizona farmers who rely on Mexican workers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a16474ccfe98f90163d6038cc1a9c6df73bdc563fa21f1698ba37bd37e557770</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T12:28:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261030-scared-of-crossing-the-border-the-arizona-farmers-who-rely-on-mexican-workers--23b97d7329e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261030-scared-of-crossing-the-border-the-arizona-farmers-who-rely-on-mexican-workers" /><summary type="html">The vast produce farms of Yuma County, Arizona, rely heavily on foreign workers who cross the border every day from Mexico. John Boelts, a farmer and staunch supporter of US President Donald Trump, praises the administration’s strict border controls – though he says that competing Republican factions have complicated efforts to hire foreign labourers.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US midterms: With deep-red states now in play, could blue wave redraw America's political landscape?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5674b0f0d31f1e1aac7a17b23ed9977994bc1c248dc5435dcac28fd3cc0a426d</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T09:30:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-with-deep-red-states-now-in-play-could-blue-wave-redraw-america-s-political-landscape--e432c3d01e5a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-with-deep-red-states-now-in-play-could-blue-wave-redraw-america-s-political-landscape" /><summary type="html">With the US approaching a potentially consequential midterm election, the political landscape appears to be shifting. Alison Sargent is pleased to welcome Dr Richard Johnson, Senior Lecturer in US Politics &amp; Policy at Queen Mary University of London, who examines the prospect of a sweeping Democratic victory. He argues that the party could achieve gains of a magnitude not seen since Barack Obama's historic presidential election in 2008. Johnson sees a combination of Democratic enthusiasm, and growing support among independents, white college-educated voters and Latinos, and signs of defections from Donald Trump's fiercely loyal electoral coalition.</summary></entry><entry><title>Michigan's El-Sayed targeted by Republicans in midterms race: Will the religion card work?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:180e3d0b9217459f4b64516ef56ceb8867e70d7c6cb26e261d52a2a58dee85de</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T19:31:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261029-michigan-s-el-sayed-targeted-by-republicans-in-midterms-race-will-the-religion-card-work--09b7ffd28c6e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261029-michigan-s-el-sayed-targeted-by-republicans-in-midterms-race-will-the-religion-card-work" /><summary type="html">What in the name of political free speech is off limits? Can you say whatever you want on the campaign trail, no matter how false or racist it is?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Lt. Gen. Ben Hodges accuses Hegseth of 'getting rid of people who may have the courage to push back'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d5b3049c4c7f6270c39c2b6adec1acd44693e2b65f9bc8f825249fa29f3693ec</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T18:09:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/lt-gen-ben-hodges-accuses-hegseth-of-getting-rid-of-people-who-may-have-the-courage-to-push-back--e4aa5af8da14.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/lt-gen-ben-hodges-accuses-hegseth-of-getting-rid-of-people-who-may-have-the-courage-to-push-back" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye welcomes Lt. General (ret.) Ben Hodges, former commander of US Army Europe and NATO Allied Land Command. The dismissal of senior military officers without public explanation raises fundamental questions about institutional trust and the relationship between civilian authority and military leadership. For General Hodges, the reported firing of Lt. General Brett Sylvia reflects a potentially troubling pattern within the Pentagon under Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth. Equally striking is his criticism of the reluctance of retired senior commanders to speak publicly against policies they consider damaging. Hodges said he was "disappointed and surprised" by the limited public resistance among former four-star generals.</summary></entry><entry><title>Flavio Bolsonaro’s great escape: Is this the beginning of the end for ‘Bolsonarism’?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:498bd8c375744efb788a890a694a404638b05c4b6ed4ca5a5df41622edd6287e</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T16:19:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261029-flavio-bolsonaro-s-great-escape-is-this-the-beginning-of-the-end-for-bolsonarism--f513ed731885.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261029-flavio-bolsonaro-s-great-escape-is-this-the-beginning-of-the-end-for-bolsonarism" /><summary type="html">The Brazilian election results had barely been announced before the defeated presidential candidate, Flavio Bolsonaro, packed his bags and fled with his family to the United States. The move may have dealt a serious blow to the already tarnished family brand, but does it spell the end for “Bolsonarism”?</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Ireland opens arms to Americans fleeing US President Donald Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a7cdd676ea85700769ab08974ec922f574f3bd86a5b5ba9b009587678049bff2</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T15:31:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-ireland-opens-arms-to-americans-fleeing-us-president-donald-trump--33ce35fb957c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-ireland-opens-arms-to-americans-fleeing-us-president-donald-trump" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of US citizens have fled the United States since Donald Trump's return to power two years ago. Given the language and a shared history, Ireland has been among the top choices for Americans looking for an alternative. FRANCE 24's team reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Midterms: Donald Trump and Barack Obama make closing pitches</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9a8bc4d92fa6e75009ffda9fe83d76a25ff37ddc2b5e7d40300070aaeaa7b841</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T14:57:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-us-midterms-donald-trump-and-barack-obama-make-closing-pitches--51abaa1b21c1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-us-midterms-donald-trump-and-barack-obama-make-closing-pitches" /><summary type="html">In the United States, Democrats are turning to Barack Obama to rally voters ahead of the midterm elections, a crucial test that could shape the remainder of Donald Trump's presidency. The former president has addressed three campaign rallies this week, with the latest one in Atlanta, Georgia. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Angela Diffley has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Why is Donald Trump avoiding the Epstein case at all costs?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d434ee70b04b5bdf6efa4e840ddd97fe5d87c0ba6d3f86d00ee6225385da31d5</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T14:37:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-why-is-donald-trump-avoiding-the-epstein-case-at-all-costs--926236f51e51.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-why-is-donald-trump-avoiding-the-epstein-case-at-all-costs" /><summary type="html">The midterm elections campaign is in full swing in the United States, but Donald Trump is doing his utmost to avoid one subject: the Epstein Files. On January 30, the US Department of Justice published the court records relating to the Epstein case. At FRANCE 24, two of our journalists, Samia Metheni and Ava Luquet, delve into the 3 million documents to understand how Epstein's network operated. What did they find looking through the documents and what impact do they still have on Trump? Ava Luquet answered François Picard's questions.</summary></entry><entry><title>USA: Barack Obama slams Donald Trump in final midterm push</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:798a24eca7f045d28898ed9b6902d299d38116670a5e39053af16a23d4dd15c9</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T12:28:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-usa-barack-obama-slams-donald-trump-in-final-midterm-push--e90924907de5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-usa-barack-obama-slams-donald-trump-in-final-midterm-push" /><summary type="html">Just five days before the US midterm elections, former president Barack Obama came to Georgia in a show of support to Senator Jon Ossoff in tthe midterm elections. Obama commented on the reaction of Trump's administration to a joke he had made the day before. "He was very upset about the Cheesecake Factory comments", Obama said. "They mobilized a whole-of-government response to that joke. Not to inflation, but to that joke." As the election is getting closer, polls point to a possible Democratic majority in the House.</summary></entry><entry><title>Flavio Bolsonaro claims he is Brazil's true leader after fleeing to US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9452d1c24affb9251f925979627a4fe13411b001d03dd513f89eaa00d6b403e3</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T22:15:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261028-flavio-bolsonaro-claims-he-is-brazil-s-true-leader-after-fleeing-to-us--c0db04b9b21d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261028-flavio-bolsonaro-claims-he-is-brazil-s-true-leader-after-fleeing-to-us" /><summary type="html">Brazil's defeated far-right presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro insisted on Wednesday he is his country's rightful leader after arriving in the United States to start a self-imposed exile. Bolsonaro's defiance on fleeing to Florida signalled continued upheaval for Brazil, where leftist President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva won a dramatic run-off election on Sunday.</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Flavio Bolsonaro claims he is Brazil's true leader after fleeing to US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd8c4eb4fd10c13457286dafe5eed21c7546dffd4cec123f1fb33178bce2e303</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T22:13:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/flavio-bolsonaro-claims-he-is-brazil-s-true-leader-after-fleeing-to-us--368e600dc388.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/flavio-bolsonaro-claims-he-is-brazil-s-true-leader-after-fleeing-to-us" /><summary type="html">Brazil's defeated far-right presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro insisted on Wednesday he is his country's rightful leader after arriving in the United States to start a self-imposed exile. Bolsonaro's defiance on fleeing to Florida signalled continued upheaval for Brazil, where leftist President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva won a dramatic run-off election on Sunday.
 
FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Fabio de Sa e Silva, Associate Professor of International Studies at the University of Oklahoma. He says that an attempt by Bolsonaro to turn a domestic dispute into a wider international issue "will not be successful", explaining that he is likely going to be "losing the grip of the opposition, there is a vacuum now that others will seek to occupy" and that it's unlikely the United States will "get involved into questioning the results of the Brazilian election".</summary></entry><entry><title>Top US federal judge who handled 9/11, Trump, Maduro cases dies aged 92</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4a6b36ffb2a18a3f308ead0aa812224b741b9e594a31259ef356d8fc210363b1</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T20:22:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261028-top-us-federal-judge-who-handled-9-11-trump-maduro-cases-dies-aged-92--a0e3ae1d91ad.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261028-top-us-federal-judge-who-handled-9-11-trump-maduro-cases-dies-aged-92" /><summary type="html">Alvin Hellerstein, a top US judge who was handling the trial against deposed Venezuelan leader Nicholas Maduro and previously oversaw lawsuits stemming from the September 11 attacks on the World Trade Centre and multiple cases involving President Donald Trump, died on Wednesday aged 92.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Bolsonaro's escape to the US: How it happened</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d7613acc1ad6cf4d0bbd5dcad26c6e655ac11a33a2f0cf87057cafff86eae23</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T20:06:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/bolsonaro-s-escape-to-the-us-how-it-happened--f71fff4a9188.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/bolsonaro-s-escape-to-the-us-how-it-happened" /><summary type="html">Brazil's defeated right-wing presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro arrived in Florida by private plane Wednesday after fleeing his country in defiance of a court order to surrender his passport. Bolsonaro, who lost a runoff election to incumbent Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva on Sunday, is under investigation in Brazil for alleged corruption and money laundering and, with his defeat, is set to lose parliamentary immunity. FRANCE 24's international affairs editor Kethevane Gorjestani explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Bolsonaro flees Brazil for US after election defeat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:432d7b46cd0c040113b9f4cdaf5a5d29c52fbdfbb397562331f02aaa0b47bae4</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T19:44:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/bolsonaro-flees-brazil-for-us-after-election-defeat--be6ab88c3a49.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/bolsonaro-flees-brazil-for-us-after-election-defeat" /><summary type="html">Flavio Bolsonaro's clandestine escape to the United States bewildered Brazil and triggered a frantic search for his whereabouts. The Supreme Court had ordered the son of jailed ex-leader Jair Bolsonaro to forfeit his passports after his electoral loss on Sunday, amid fears he would leave the country due to ongoing investigations against him. But the defeated right-wing presidential candidate failed to hand them in, choosing instead to flee to the US via Argentina and Ecuador. FRANCE 24's Tim Vickery reports from Rio de Janeiro.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Si, se puede': US civil rights icon Dolores Huerta dies at 96</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc1b915efece1ab0459f7840e79185a95d10df1b00786fdd72171b65420c279c</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T17:49:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261028-si-se-puede-us-civil-rights-icon-dolores-huerta-dies-96--8714b827ca22.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261028-si-se-puede-us-civil-rights-icon-dolores-huerta-dies-96" /><summary type="html">Influential US labour union co-founder, feminist, and civil rights icon Dolores Huerta died on Wednesday in Bakersfield, California, her family said. Credited with coining the enduring "Si, se puede!" rallying cry later adapted by former US president Barack Obama, Huerta continued her activism on race, poverty, LGBTQ and women's rights issues until the last months of her life.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US grants visa to defeated Brazilian presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1ecb8dcea79d45ed247e9bf75689636db8e1983c375ed2b16ff2b7c345edcd6e</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T17:00:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-us-grants-visa-to-defeated-brazilian-presidential-candidate-flavio-bolsonaro--19875dc44dd0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-us-grants-visa-to-defeated-brazilian-presidential-candidate-flavio-bolsonaro" /><summary type="html">Brazil's defeated presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro and his immediate family landed in Miami, Florida on Wednesday after he refused to surrender his passports as ordered by his country's Supreme Court in connection with a money-laundering probe. The US State Department on Tuesday announced it had granted entry visas to the senator and his family. France 24's Kethevane Gorjestani explains.</summary></entry></feed>
